Use this display when A and B are nonbottom.
\[
  \AxiomC{}
  \RightLabel{$\pi_1$}
  \Deduce$\Gamma_1' \fCenter !B \lif !A$
  \AxiomC{}
  \RightLabel{$\pi_2$}
  \Deduce$\Gamma_2' \fCenter !B$
  \Axiom$!A \fCenter !A$
  \RightLabel{\LeftR{\lif}}
  \BinaryInf$!B \lif !A, \Gamma_2' \fCenter !A$
  \RightLabel{\Cut}
  \BinaryInf$\Gamma_1', \Gamma_2' \fCenter !A$
  \DisplayProof
  \]
If A is bottom but B is not, replace the A-identity axiom by bottom proves empty and keep both following conclusions empty.

\[
  \Axiom$!A \fCenter !A$
  \RightLabel{\RightR{\lnot}}
  \UnaryInf$\fCenter !A, \lnot !A$
  \AxiomC{}
  \RightLabel{$\pi_1$}
  \Deduce$\lnot !A, \Gamma' \fCenter $
  \RightLabel{\Cut}
  \BinaryInf$\Gamma' \fCenter !A$
  \DisplayProof
  \]
If the conclusion A is bottom, cut the resulting bottom-succedent proof with bottom proves empty to meet the theorem invariant.
